h3 2.3.2 Boolean attributes
text A number of attributes are . The presence of a boolean attribute on an element represents the true value, and the absence of the attribute represents the false value.
text boolean attributes
text If the attribute is present, its value must either be the empty string or a value that is an  match for the attribute's canonical name, with no leading or trailing whitespace.
link "ASCII case-insensitive" https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive
text "The values \"true\" and \"false\" are not allowed on boolean attributes. To represent a false value, the attribute has to be omitted altogether." success
text Here is an example of a checkbox that is checked and disabled. The  and  attributes are the boolean attributes.
row
  link checked input.html#attr-input-checked
  link "disabled" form-control-infrastructure.html#attr-fe-disabled
text Cheese
card
  text <
  text label success
  text ><
  text input success
  text type primary
  text =
  text checkbox warning
  text checked primary
  text name primary
  text =
  text cheese warning
  text "disabled" primary
  text >
  text </
  text label success
  text >
text This could be equivalently written as this:
text Cheese
card
  text <
