  text name primary
  text =
  text cheese warning
  text "disabled" primary
  text =
  text "disabled" warning
  text >
  text </
  text label success
  text >
text You can also mix styles; the following is still equivalent:
text Cheese
card
  text <
  text label success
  text ><
  text input success
  text type primary
  text =
  text 'checkbox' warning
  text checked primary
  text name primary
  text =
  text cheese warning
  text "disabled" primary
  text =
  text "\"\"" warning
  text >
  text </
  text label success
  text >
h3 2.3.3 Keywords and enumerated attributes
text Some attributes, called , take on a finite set of states. The state for such an attribute is derived by combining the attribute's value, a set of keyword/state mappings, and three possible special states that can also be given in the specification of the attribute. These special states are the , the , and the .
text enumerated attributes
text invalid value default
text missing value default
text empty value default
text Multiple keywords can map to the same state. success
text To determine the state of an attribute, use the following steps:
text If the attribute is not specified:
text If the attribute has a  state defined, then return that  state.
row
  link "missing value default" #missing-value-default
  link "missing value default" #missing-value-default
text Otherwise, return no state.
text If the attribute's value is an  match for one of the keywords defined for the attribute, then return the state represented by that keyword.
link "ASCII case-insensitive" https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive
text If the attribute has an  state defined and the attribute's value is the empty string, then return that  state.
row
  link "empty value default" #empty-value-default
  link "empty value default" #empty-value-default
text If the attribute has an  state defined, then return that  state.
row
  link "invalid value default" #invalid-value-default
  link "invalid value default" #invalid-value-default
text Return no state.
text For authoring conformance purposes, if an enumerated attribute is specified, the attribute's value must be one of:
text An  match for one of the conforming keywords for that attribute, with no leading or trailing whitespace.
link "ASCII case-insensitive" https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive
text The empty string and the attribute must have an  defined.
link "empty value default" #empty-value-default
text For  purposes, states which have any keywords mapping to them are said to have a . This is determined as follows:
row
  link reflection common-dom-interfaces.html#reflect
  text canonical keyword
text If there is only one keyword mapping to the given state, then it is that keyword.
text If there is only one conforming keyword mapping to the given state, then it is that conforming keyword.
text If there are two conforming keywords mapping to the given state, and one is the empty string, then the canonical keyword will be the conforming keyword that is not the empty string.
text Otherwise, the canonical keyword for the state will be explicitly given in the specification for the attribute.
