h3 2.3.4.3 Floating-point numbers
text A string is a  if it consists of:
text valid floating-point number
text Optionally, a U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS character (-).
text One or both of the following, in the given order:
text A series of one or more .
link "ASCII digits" https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-digit
text Both of the following, in the given order:
text A single U+002E FULL STOP character (.).
text A series of one or more .
link "ASCII digits" https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-digit
text Optionally:
text Either a U+0065 LATIN SMALL LETTER E character (e) or a U+0045 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER E character (E).
text Optionally, a U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS character (-) or U+002B PLUS SIGN character (+).
text A series of one or more .
link "ASCII digits" https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-digit
text A  represents the number obtained by multiplying the significand by ten raised to the power of the exponent, where the significand is the first number, interpreted as base ten (including the decimal point and the number after the decimal point, if any, and interpreting the significand as a negative number if the whole string starts with a U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS character (-) and the number is not zero), and where the exponent is the number after the E, if any (interpreted as a negative number if there is a U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS character (-) between the E and the number and the number is not zero, or else ignoring a U+002B PLUS SIGN character (+) between the E and the number if there is one). If there is no E, then the exponent is treated as zero.
link "valid floating-point number" #valid-floating-point-number
text The Infinity and Not-a-Number (NaN) values are not . success
link "valid floating-point numbers" #valid-floating-point-number
